<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Model-based reinforcement learning (RL) achieves superior sample efficiency by learning dynamics models that enable planning and simulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chua et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Janner et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hansen et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hafner et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. But a fundamental challenge remains: <span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">how should agents explore when their world models are uncertain?</span> Existing deep RL methods rely on heuristic uncertainty quantification, including, for example, ensemble disagreement <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pathak et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shyam et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, prediction error bonuses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pathak et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, and variational inference in Bayesian neural networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Houthooft et al., 2016</a>)</cite>. These strategies that have good empirical results lack direct connections to the requirements of optimal exploration.
Multi-armed bandits (MABs) offer a precise characterization of exploration difficulty through regret lower bounds: optimal algorithms must accumulate sufficient statistical evidence to distinguish the true environment from <em id="S1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">confusing instances</em>—plausible alternative models that are statistically similar to the true model yet require different optimal actions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai and Robbins, 1985</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burnetas and Katehakis, 1996</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burnetas and Katehakis, 1997</a>)</cite>.
Exploration strategies that explicitly construct and resolve such confusing instances achieve <span id="S1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">asymptotically</span> optimal regret in various settings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Honda and Takemura, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pesquerel and Maillard, 2022</a>)</cite>. However, finding these instances in practice, especially for continuous or high-dimensional domains with learned models, remains unexplored and NP-Hard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radji and Maillard, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boone and Maillard, 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Research problem.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The central computational challenge is identifying the <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">most</em> confusing instance: the alternative model that is statistically closest to the learned model while still inducing a different optimal policy. For general Markov decision processes, this search is NP-hard, making optimal exploration seemingly intractable in high-dimensional state spaces.
In this paper, we investigate this problem empirically for probabilistic world models based on variational autoencoder (VAE) architectures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ha and Schmidhuber, 2018</a>)</cite>. We formalize the search for the most confusing instance as a constrained optimization problem, via Lagrangian relaxation, introducing the <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">suboptimality cost</em>, that is, the minimal log-likelihood ratio required to reverse policy rankings between the learned model and a confusing alternative. Our key empirical finding is a relationship between model quality and confusion resistance: better-trained models have higher suboptimality costs. This intuitive relationship suggests that suboptimality cost is related to model uncertainty, offering a promising approach to quantifying exploration difficulty that paves the way for new exploration strategies in deep model-based RL.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Background and setting.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider episodic reinforcement learning in continuous state and action spaces <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with reward function <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton et al., 1998</a>)</cite>. A learned world model <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> approximates environment dynamics through probabilistic transitions <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, trained on observed environment data. We assume these transitions are differentiable with respect to <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, enabling gradient-based optimization.
Given a starting state <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\pi}(s_{0};M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi}(s_{0};M)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expected return of policy <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> under model <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, as</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\pi}(s_{0};M)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim M,\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R(s_{t},a_{t})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi}(s_{0};M)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim M,\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R(s_{t},a_{t})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(s_{0},a_{0},s_{1},\ldots,s_{T-1},a_{T-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(s_{0},a_{0},s_{1},\ldots,s_{T-1},a_{T-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is a trajectory of fixed horizon <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> optimal under the reference model <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> suboptimal under <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};M_{\theta})&gt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};M_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};M_{\theta})&gt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};M_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Most Confusing Instance Search</h2>

<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Confusing Instance)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given reference model <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with optimal policy <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and suboptimal policy <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sub</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> at state <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, a model <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}=M_{\tilde{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}=M_{\tilde{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">confusing instance</em> if it is statistically close to <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> yet inverts the policy ranking:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})&lt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M}),\ \text{and KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})=\underset{{\tau\sim M_{\theta},\pi^{*}}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{P_{\theta}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})}{P_{\tilde{\theta}}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})}\right],\text{ is small}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sub</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and KL</mtext><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">τ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is small</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})&lt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M}),\ \text{and KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})=\underset{{\tau\sim M_{\theta},\pi^{*}}}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\frac{P_{\theta}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})}{P_{\tilde{\theta}}(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})}\right],\text{ is small}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The last quantity represents the expected log-likelihood ratio of trajectories generated by <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> under the two models. A small (minimal) divergence implies we cannot reliably distinguish between <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}</annotation></semantics></math> by executing only the optimal policy; yet the models prescribe different optimal behaviors.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Suboptimality Cost)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Among all confusing instances, we seek the one that is statistically closest to the reference model. The <em id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">suboptimality cost</em> is the infimum of KL divergences over all confusing instances:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{K}(s_{0},\pi^{*},\pi_{\text{sub}})=\inf_{\tilde{\theta}}\left\{\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}}):V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})&lt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sub</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sub</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}(s_{0},\pi^{*},\pi_{\text{sub}})=\inf_{\tilde{\theta}}\left\{\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}}):V_{\pi^{*}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})&lt;V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(s_{0};\widetilde{M})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This cost quantifies the minimal statistical evidence needed to distinguish which policy is truly superior. RL theory indicates that algorithms must accumulate at least <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> nats to avoid linear regret. Thus, <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> measures model uncertainty for exploration: low values indicate the model is easily confused and requires more data, while high values indicate alternative explanations are statistically distant, making the model reliable for decision-making.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimization.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finding (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In Definition 2 (Suboptimality Cost). ‣ 2 Most Confusing Instance Search ‣ How Hard is it to Confuse a World Model?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is a challenging constrained optimization: the objective involves expectations over stochastic trajectories, and the constraint depends on value functions that themselves require trajectory rollouts. While this problem is generally NP-hard, the differentiable structure of neural world models enables tractable local optimization via gradient descent. We address these challenges through Lagrangian relaxation and sampling-based gradient estimation:</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\tilde{\theta},\lambda)=\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})+\lambda\max\left(0,V_{\pi^{*}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})-V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mtext>KL</mtext><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\tilde{\theta},\lambda)=\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})+\lambda\max\left(0,V_{\pi^{*}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})-V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lagrange multiplier. The algorithm alternates between:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Primal)}\quad\tilde{\theta}^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(Primal)</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Primal)}\quad\tilde{\theta}^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\tilde{\theta}^{(k)}-\alpha_{\theta}\nabla_{\tilde{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\tilde{\theta}^{(k)},\lambda^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\tilde{\theta}^{(k)}-\alpha_{\theta}\nabla_{\tilde{\theta}}\mathcal{L}(\tilde{\theta}^{(k)},\lambda^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Dual)}\quad\lambda^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(Dual)</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Dual)}\quad\lambda^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\max\left(0,\lambda^{(k)}+\alpha_{\lambda}\cdot c(\tilde{\theta}^{(k)})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\max\left(0,\lambda^{(k)}+\alpha_{\lambda}\cdot c(\tilde{\theta}^{(k)})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\tilde{\theta})=V_{\pi^{*}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})-V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\tilde{\theta})=V_{\pi^{*}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})-V_{\pi_{\text{sub}}}(M_{\tilde{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
When the constraint is violated (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), the multiplier <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> increases, penalizing the objective more heavily. When satisfied (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), we record the current KL as a candidate for <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. The infimum is the smallest KL achieved among all feasible iterates. An analogy can be made with policy gradient algorithms with KL regularization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite>: instead of optimizing the policy, we optimize a world model.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Numerical Experiments</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our framework applies to any differentiable probabilistic model, we instantiate it for variational autoencoder world models in our experiments due to their straightforward implementation and interpretable latent representations. A VAE world model decomposes as <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}=(\phi,\psi,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}=(\phi,\psi,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an encoder mapping states to latent codes <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim q_{\phi}(z|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim q_{\phi}(z|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> models the latent dynamics <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\psi}(z^{\prime}|z,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\psi}(z^{\prime}|z,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is a decoder reconstructing states <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim p_{\xi}(s|z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim p_{\xi}(s|z)</annotation></semantics></math>. We focus on fully observable environments in our experiments, so our model uses a feedforward architecture without recurrent components.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Compute Suboptimality Cost in VAE</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Reference model <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}=(\phi,\psi,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}=(\phi,\psi,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, policies <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*},\pi_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*},\pi_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math>, horizon <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Suboptimality cost <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Initialize: <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\psi}\leftarrow\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\psi}\leftarrow\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leftarrow 1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leftarrow 1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}\leftarrow+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}\leftarrow+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> initial states: <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}^{(n)}\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}^{(n)}\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            Encode: <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}^{(n)}=\phi(s_{0}^{(n)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}^{(n)}=\phi(s_{0}^{(n)})</annotation></semantics></math> (deterministic for frozen encoder)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Rollout <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\tilde{\theta}}=(\phi,\tilde{\psi},\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\tilde{\theta}}=(\phi,\tilde{\psi},\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>: generate trajectory <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{*(n)}=\{(z_{t},a_{t},r_{t})\}_{t=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{*(n)}=\{(z_{t},a_{t},r_{t})\}_{t=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             Rollout <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\tilde{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\tilde{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>: generate trajectory <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{sub}}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>sub</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{sub}}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Compute average KL: <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{NT}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\text{KL}(p_{\psi}(\cdot|z_{t}^{(n)},a_{t}^{(n)})\|p_{\tilde{\psi}}(\cdot|z_{t}^{(n)},a_{t}^{(n)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext>KL</mtext><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\text{KL}}=\frac{1}{NT}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\text{KL}(p_{\psi}(\cdot|z_{t}^{(n)},a_{t}^{(n)})\|p_{\tilde{\psi}}(\cdot|z_{t}^{(n)},a_{t}^{(n)}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            Compute average returns: <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{V^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n}\sum_{t}r_{t}^{*(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{V^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n}\sum_{t}r_{t}^{*(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{V_{\text{sub}}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n}\sum_{t}r_{t}^{\text{sub},(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mtext>sub</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{V_{\text{sub}}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n}\sum_{t}r_{t}^{\text{sub},(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            Constraint violation: <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\overline{V^{*}}-\overline{V_{\text{sub}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\overline{V^{*}}-\overline{V_{\text{sub}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}\leftarrow\min(\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}},\overline{\text{KL}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext>KL</mtext><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}\leftarrow\min(\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}},\overline{\text{KL}})</annotation></semantics></math> {Record feasible KL}

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            Update dynamics: <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\psi}\leftarrow\tilde{\psi}-\alpha_{\psi}\nabla_{\tilde{\psi}}[\overline{\text{KL}}+\lambda\cdot\max(0,c)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext>KL</mtext><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\psi}\leftarrow\tilde{\psi}-\alpha_{\psi}\nabla_{\tilde{\psi}}[\overline{\text{KL}}+\lambda\cdot\max(0,c)]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
            Update multiplier: <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leftarrow\max(0,\lambda+\eta\cdot c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leftarrow\max(0,\lambda+\eta\cdot c)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{\text{best}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>World Model Architecture and Training</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our VAE-based world model consists of three components:</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Encoder</span> <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>: Two-layer MLP with hidden dimension 64 and tanh activations, mapping observations <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> to latent codes <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{z}\in\{32,64\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{z}\in\{32,64\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamics</span> <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>: Two-layer MLP with hidden dimension 64, taking concatenated latent-action pairs <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z,a)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z,a)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}+2}</annotation></semantics></math> and outputting Gaussian parameters <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{\psi},\sigma_{\psi}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{\psi},\sigma_{\psi}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for the next latent state. We parameterize variance as <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=(\text{softplus}(\text{logvar}_{\text{raw}})+10^{-8})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>softplus</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logvar</mtext><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=(\text{softplus}(\text{logvar}_{\text{raw}})+10^{-8})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decoder</span> <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>: Two-layer MLP with hidden dimension 64 and tanh activations, reconstructing state differences <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta s\in\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta s\in\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> from latent codes.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We train on 50,000 transitions collected via random exploration (500 trajectories of 200 steps each, with action repeat sampled uniformly). The loss combines reconstruction and KL regularization:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{train}}=\mathbb{E}_{(s,a,\Delta s)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\|\Delta\hat{s}-\Delta s\|^{2}\right]+0.01\cdot\text{KL}(q_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\|\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>s</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{train}}=\mathbb{E}_{(s,a,\Delta s)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\|\Delta\hat{s}-\Delta s\|^{2}\right]+0.01\cdot\text{KL}(q_{\phi}(\cdot|s)\|\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Training proceeds for 500 epochs with the Adam optimizer (learning rate <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>) and batch size 256. We save checkpoints at epochs 100, 200, 300, 400, and 500, providing a spectrum of model qualities from under-trained (high uncertainty) to well-trained (low uncertainty).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Confusing Instance Search Implementation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate dynamical uncertainty from representational artifacts, we <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">freeze</span> the encoder <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and decoder <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, perturbing only the latent dynamics <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures the confusing instance operates in the same representational space, making comparisons meaningful, and avoiding trivial confusion of the model by distorting the representation itself.
For Gaussian latent dynamics <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\psi}(z^{\prime}|z,a)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\psi}(z,a),\text{diag}(\sigma_{\psi}^{2}(z,a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\psi}(z^{\prime}|z,a)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{\psi}(z,a),\text{diag}(\sigma_{\psi}^{2}(z,a)))</annotation></semantics></math>, the pointwise KL divergence has closed form:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{KL}(p_{\psi}\|p_{\tilde{\psi}})=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d_{z}}\left[\log\frac{\tilde{\sigma}_{\psi,i}^{2}}{\sigma_{\psi,i}^{2}}+\frac{\sigma_{\psi,i}^{2}+(\mu_{\psi,i}-\tilde{\mu}_{\psi,i})^{2}}{\tilde{\sigma}_{\psi,i}^{2}}-1\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KL}(p_{\psi}\|p_{\tilde{\psi}})=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d_{z}}\left[\log\frac{\tilde{\sigma}_{\psi,i}^{2}}{\sigma_{\psi,i}^{2}}+\frac{\sigma_{\psi,i}^{2}+(\mu_{\psi,i}-\tilde{\mu}_{\psi,i})^{2}}{\tilde{\sigma}_{\psi,i}^{2}}-1\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We approximate trajectory-level KL by averaging pointwise KL along rollouts:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim M_{\tilde{\theta}},\pi^{*}}\left[\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\text{KL}(p_{\psi}(\cdot|z_{t},a_{t})\|p_{\tilde{\psi}}(\cdot|z_{t},a_{t}))\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>KL</mtext><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KL}_{T}^{\pi^{*}}(M_{\theta}\|M_{\tilde{\theta}})\approx\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim M_{\tilde{\theta}},\pi^{*}}\left[\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\text{KL}(p_{\psi}(\cdot|z_{t},a_{t})\|p_{\tilde{\psi}}(\cdot|z_{t},a_{t}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We optimize confusing instances for 2500 iterations with <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=128</annotation></semantics></math> trajectory samples per iteration. The learning rate for dynamics parameters follows a linear schedule from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, with gradient clipping at max norm 1.0. The Lagrange multiplier <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to 1.0 and updated with step size <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the Adam optimizer and save checkpoints every 100 iterations. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Numerical Experiments ‣ How Hard is it to Confuse a World Model?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> presents the complete procedure for computing suboptimality cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Task and Policy Construction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on a U-shaped maze environment with a <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math> grid structure from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radji (2025)</a></cite>. The agent has a continuous state representation (2D position and velocity) and must navigate to a fixed goal location. We use a dense reward signal equal to the negative Manhattan distance between the agent’s position and the goal.
We construct two policy-maze pairs to define optimal and suboptimal behaviors. The optimal policy <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed via breadth-first search (BFS) on the original discretized U-Maze, following the shortest path. The suboptimal policy <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by first moving one wall in the maze to create an alternative layout, then computing BFS on this modified maze. When executed in the original U-Maze, this policy follows a longer route and is thus suboptimal. Both policies have been augmented with Gaussian noise of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> to introduce stochasticity during rollouts. Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.3 Task and Policy Construction ‣ 3 Numerical Experiments ‣ How Hard is it to Confuse a World Model?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the maze configurations used to construct the two policies.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="232.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 378.23 232.79" width="378.23"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,232.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.14,0) translate(0,47.21)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 29.34 171.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.21em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="98.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Original Maze</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 157.48 0 M 0 31.5 L 157.48 31.5 M 0 62.99 L 157.48 62.99 M 0 94.49 L 157.48 94.49 M 0 125.98 L 157.48 125.98 M 0 157.47 L 157.48 157.47 M 0 0 L 0 157.48 M 31.5 0 L 31.5 157.48 M 62.99 0 L 62.99 157.48 M 94.49 0 L 94.49 157.48 M 125.98 0 L 125.98 157.48 M 157.47 0 L 157.47 157.48 M 157.48 157.48"></path></g><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 31.5 L 157.48 31.5 L 157.48 0 Z M 157.48 31.5"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 31.5 M 0 31.5 L 0 62.99 L 31.5 62.99 L 31.5 31.5 Z M 31.5 62.99"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 125.98 31.5 M 125.98 31.5 L 125.98 62.99 L 157.48 62.99 L 157.48 31.5 Z M 157.48 62.99"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 62.99 M 0 62.99 L 0 94.49 L 31.5 94.49 L 31.5 62.99 Z M 31.5 94.49"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 31.5 62.99 M 31.5 62.99 L 31.5 94.49 L 62.99 94.49 L 62.99 62.99 Z M 62.99 94.49"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 62.99 62.99 M 62.99 62.99 L 62.99 94.49 L 94.49 94.49 L 94.49 62.99 Z M 94.49 94.49"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 125.98 62.99 M 125.98 62.99 L 125.98 94.49 L 157.48 94.49 L 157.48 62.99 Z M 157.48 94.49"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 94.49 M 0 94.49 L 0 125.98 L 31.5 125.98 L 31.5 94.49 Z M 31.5 125.98"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 125.98 94.49 M 125.98 94.49 L 125.98 125.98 L 157.48 125.98 L 157.48 94.49 Z M 157.48 125.98"></path><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 125.98 M 0 125.98 L 0 157.48 L 157.48 157.48 L 157.48 125.98 Z M 157.48 157.48"></path><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3FFB3;" fill="#B3FFB3"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 59.21 47.24 C 59.21 53.85 53.85 59.21 47.24 59.21 C 40.64 59.21 35.28 53.85 35.28 47.24 C 35.28 40.64 40.64 35.28 47.24 35.28 C 53.85 35.28 59.21 40.64 59.21 47.24 Z M 47.24 47.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 43.4 42.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="7.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">S</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFB3B3;" fill="#FFB3B3"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 60.29 110.24 C 60.29 117.44 54.45 123.28 47.24 123.28 C 40.04 123.28 34.2 117.44 34.2 110.24 C 34.2 103.03 40.04 97.19 47.24 97.19 C 54.45 97.19 60.29 103.03 60.29 110.24 Z M 47.24 110.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 41.82 105.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text">G</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#4D4DFF;" color="#4D4DFF" stroke-width="1.5pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;" fill="#4D4DFF" stroke="#4D4DFF"><path style="fill:none" d="M 47.24 47.24 L 78.74 47.24 L 110.24 47.24 L 110.24 78.74 L 110.24 110.24 L 78.74 110.24 L 49.32 110.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;" fill="#4D4DFF" stroke="#4D4DFF" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 48.28 110.24)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -4.7 6.07 C -3.85 2.43 -1.93 0.71 0 0 C -1.93 -0.71 -3.85 -2.43 -4.7 -6.07"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 246.87 168.67)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="104.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modified Maze</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 220.47 0 M 220.47 0 L 377.95 0 M 220.47 31.5 L 377.95 31.5 M 220.47 62.99 L 377.95 62.99 M 220.47 94.49 L 377.95 94.49 M 220.47 125.98 L 377.95 125.98 M 220.47 157.47 L 377.95 157.47 M 220.47 0 L 220.47 157.48 M 251.97 0 L 251.97 157.48 M 283.47 0 L 283.47 157.48 M 314.96 0 L 314.96 157.48 M 346.46 0 L 346.46 157.48 M 377.94 0 L 377.94 157.48 M 377.95 157.48"></path></g><path style="stroke:none" d="M 220.47 0 M 220.47 0 L 220.47 31.5 L 3